se  are these are the most important issues  that I think the Republican candidates  are showing that we have common sense  solutions to and as I've traveled around  the nation and had a chance to visit  with Republican governor candidates what  we're also able to demonstrate is that  States run by Republican Governors have  outperformed States run by Democrat  governors in an extraordinary rate  Economic Development out outcomes in  schools small business growth I mean the  reality of course is that even a state  like Virginia where under the previous  Democrat leadership there were 47th in  the nation in job recovery coming out of  the pandemic and now in the last eight  months we've actually rocketed up into a  top 20 State and job recovery this is  all about common sense solutions to  these most important issues so somebody  ask you this question because you said  that this what's important are issues  that people deal with on a day-to-day  basis the Democrats would argue that  abortion is an issue that many women in  America deal with on a day-to-day basis  and it is incredibly important issue for  them let's put up on the screen latest  Washington Post ABC News poll how  Republicans and Democrats fare against  each other on all these issues the  economy Republicans with a clear lead  inflation Republicans with a clear lead  abortion it flips around the Democrats  have got about the same percentage and  then it goes on down through crime  education schools climate change and  immigration Republicans need to make  this election about bread and butter  issues because the abortion message from  the Democrats is what closed the Gap  over the long summer holiday what what  can the Republicans do in the next six  weeks to try to stretch that lead back  out again I mean it was it was it was a  bloodbath for the for the Republicans  against the Democrats until that dots  decision came out  well let me begin with the fact that  even in my election last year my  opponent tried to make the entire  election about abortion and of course  it's not something that I shied away  from I mean Virginians elected a  pro-life Governor last year of course  the reality is that is that my opponent  and the left liberal Democrats are the  ones with the extreme views it is  Extreme to promote abortion all the way  up through and including birth paid for  with taxpayer money and Virginians  expressed one clear desire to have fewer  abortions as opposed to more and that's  the idea that abortions would be  available all the way up through birth  was Radical and I think Americans  believe that as well and I think that's  the message that Republican candidates  need to carry clearly you're 100 right  as we head into the this November the  8th election and oh by the way in  Virginia we're already in early voting  voters are really focusing on those  issues that they care most about and of  course Paco book issues and runaway  inflation that really represents the  failed Biden presidency when it comes to  managing our economy crime which  represents the the fundamental belief  from Progressive liberals that you bring  fewer resources as opposed to more  resources and guess what crime goes up  and education in education as everyone  is now back in school is taking its  rightful place as a top issue we saw it  in Virginia and let's just be clear  parents matter this is not a Republican  versus Democrat issue this is a parent  issue and I think we'll continue to see  education play a huge role in the  outcome of this election Governor let me  come back to Crime which you mentioned  just a moment ago uh my colleague Katie  Pavlich one of her favorite things to do  is go on the next door app and check on  what's going on with crime in her  neighborhood and then when you listen to  the far left Democrats this is what  they're saying about crime listen here  defunding the police has to happen we  need to defund the police yes I support  the defund movement talking about  um the reduction of our NYPD budget and  defunding a six billion NYPD budget not  only do we need to defund but we need to  dismantle now that was the far left of  the left there's no question about that  President Biden has tried to come out  and say no I'm not for defunding the  police I'm for funding the police but do  they basically own what the members of  the squad said  I think they have to and the reality  when we speak with Community leaders in  commit in communities that are really  suffering a dramatic escalation in  violent crimes is they want more police  on the street they want more prosecutors  in order to keep people in jail and oh  by the way they would like more  activities for their children so that  their kids have positive things to do  and those are the kinds of things we're  pressing forward with in Virginia but by  the way the bottom line is we see a  dramatic gap between full Staffing and  current Staffing in almost every police  agency and this has to be the primary  goal is to re-establish full Staffing  and full funding for training and  equipment and personnel and that's got  to be our first step in making  communities safer and that's what we're  doing in Virginia so like all polls this  ABC News Washington Post poll uh was a  bit of a popularity contest as well  Biden's approval rating in this poll is  at 39 percent his disapproval rating is  at 53 percent and Biden has in the past  inextricably linked himself to the  Democratic party listen to how he put it  I am the Democratic party right now the  platform of the democratic department is  what I in fact approved of  poll numbers that's the sort of thing  that Republicans could put on a loop  and I think the Republicans are I mean  the reality is that we're gonna we're  gonna see Joe Biden's uh uh perception  from voters reflected in how they vote  and let's just be real inflation's at a  40-year high we're seeing the economy  all of a sudden be forcibly stalled in  order to combat it we've got challenges  in our schools where we've had dramatic  learning losses and kids have suffered  because of unforced shuttering of  schools by democrats all over the nation  we're seeing high crime and oh by the  way voters are asking one basic question  which is why would I support any of that  when in fact there are common sense  solutions to all of these issues and  that's what Republican Governors have  demonstrated that they're doing and oh  by the way that's where our Republican  congressional candidates and Senate  candidates are in fact promising that  they are going to stand up and press  forward with so so the the uh former  press secretary for president bud  jensaki has become uh remarkably candid  since she left the White House she was  on Meet the Press yesterday saying here  is the choice that voters have and  here's what it means for Democrats  listen to how she put it  if the election is about who is the most  extreme  um as we saw you know Kevin McCarthy  touch on there with Marjorie Taylor  green I'll say her name sitting over his  left side then they're going to win if  it is a referendum on the president they  will lose  so you are a candidate who was known as  a trump candidate you tacked hard toward  the middle to make sure that you didn't  alienate all of those moderate voters  and you won election in part two because  Terry McAuliffe really put not just one  foot in his mouth but both of them uh  all all the way down to his his stomach  but  what do you say to some of these  candidates out there in the Republican  Party who to many people do look like  they're on the extreme end of things  I first say that candidates need to  recognize that they have to stay true to  who they are  and that's one of the things that I was  able to do last year is establish a  platform and run consistently on it for  the entire campaign and then oh by the  way deliver on it when I was elected I  also think it's really important for  candidates 